{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1131434-converting-an-npc-to-the-technocracy","id":1131434,"title":"Converting an NPC to the Technocracy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-19T14:08:13-07:00","id":1131434,"title":"Converting an NPC to the Technocracy","content":"Hi All, I am writing here with hope that I (playing an NPC in the NWO who is likely higher up on the chain than my PC) can help convert (preferably fully voluntarily) another NPC, <b>Lieutenant Thursday</b>, over to the Technocracy. The preference is voluntary paradigm shift, but if need be, we could do something like the Processing Rote on pages 86 to 87 of the most recent NWO Book.<br /> <br /> Here is information on the target for conversion. He is currently a Lieutenant (was recently promoted partly because he was the only one without connection to a scandal, and he has Mind 3, so that probably helped too) in the Oakland Police Department. He was previously an Army Ranger. We have his full military record (I can likely ask the ST more about details on this to exploit/use it). He is a member of the Norse Branch of the Euthanatos called the &quot;Gallowsmen.&quot;<br /> <br /> He seems to be running things in this area; he has a group of underlings of his own, although I'm not sure how many of them are Awakened vs. Sleepwalkers, etc. It's possible at this point he's the only Awakened member left (one of his apprentices left the area after intentionally botching an assassination of a werewolf that Thursday had ordered, and another was killed earlier in an unintended confrontation with werewolves).<br /> <br /> Thursday is very into his own power and authority (he uses or at least used a specialized if not unique Focus for his Mind effects of a badge, and either he or his apprentice have used formal police documents done in an overly ornate way to induce Mind effects on specific readers of those documents). I also believe he has inscribed runes onto his skeleton somehow for lethal (or possibly aggravated?) damage when punching (the runes on his skeleton is something that none of the Technocrats know). Group members have used Norse Runes for effects such as immolating homeless military veterans (to send to Asgard) or inducing hypothermic death in homeless people who are useless/trouble (presumably sending them to Hel instead?).<br /> <br /> Thursday does not like werewolves, and the Sabbat had a recent Halloween 'celebration' in town that resulted in many people dying (our PC group stopped two sites from killing any more people than they already had before we got there and killed the Vampires; Thursday failed to stop some Vampires from 'playing Angry Birds' with three people against a wall, one of whom was a child). So there is likely a lot of potential hate for Reality Deviants.<br /> <br /> From the ST: his view of authority (might makes right) 1) gives an opening to the Technocrats, and 2) has prevented Thursday from viewing a distinction between himself and these other authorities.<br /> <br /> Apparently Thursday has no idea he is in danger of Technocratic conversion (either voluntary or forced if need be).<br /> <br /> Thursday was being celebrated by city government members as having improved crime rates in the city and 'solving' the homeless problem (by essentially kicking them out of Oakland), etc. etc. But the recent Sabbat incident likely will result in city government people (notably the Mayor) distancing themselves from Thursday, which might permit the NWO recruiter (the NPC I will be playing) to sidle up to Thursday as a friend with an opportunity/ &quot;new position.&quot;<br /> <br /> How would you go about bringing this guy over, preferably to the Technocracy (any convention will do, but NWO Operative preferred as the NWO is putting in the effort here) as a fully voluntary convert? There is always the fallback of the Processing Rote, but I think the voluntary convert is the greater challenge and typically of more long-term benefit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12988-imperator","name":"Imperator","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T14:42:39-07:00","id":1132398,"title":"","content":"There is a mind 4 effect that allows an NWO agent to convince people off a truth relatively easily compared to a full brainwashing.<br /> <br /> NWO agent comes in under the guise of the FBI to investigate. Lead Thursday back over all the harm Reality Deviants have done by virtue of rehashing all these cases. Priming him for the conversation where he can be offered a chance to actually make a difference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T20:32:46-07:00","id":1134343,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the response! We did something similar to that, actually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12988-imperator","name":"Imperator","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T02:31:40-07:00","id":1134405,"title":"","content":"In regards to approaching Lieutenant Thursday and making him join the Technocracy I'd recommend: honesty and respect.<br /> <br /> Present him with the resources of the Technocracy. Their goals and values. (The Precepts of Damian perhaps.) Don't paint things as too rosy - discuss the challenges and difficulties as well. Perhaps give him the opportunity to choose his future Methodology in the New World Order - maybe either the Operatives or the Watchers. (His involvement in matters of Nightfolk other than True Mages might make him a good Watcher.) Make the case that he could be an Enforcer for the Syndicate, but that you don't recommend it; considering that Thursday's recruiters are in the NWO, it would mean more logistical and practical problems in regards to placing Lieutenant Thursday in the Technocracy efficiently. (And of course it might not benefit Thursday's recruiters if he ends up in the Syndicate.)<br /> Present and discuss the Technocracy's attitude towards other True Mages, especially the Traditions. Ask him for his opinion, and prepare and adjust his possible place in the Technocracy based on what he says. Depending on the outcome, he can become someone who neutralizes and works counter to the actions of Traditions True Mages; or someone who acts as a liaison and diplomat for the Technocracy in regards to the Traditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 08-27-2017, 05:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}